checkSolver -- tests a semidefinite programming solver
******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        checkSolver(solver)
        checkSolver(solver,fun)
  * Inputs:
      * solver, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, either "M2" or "CSDP" or
        "SDPA" or "MOSEK"
      * fun, a *note function: (Macaulay2Doc)Function,, optional, one of *note
        optimize: (SemidefiniteProgramming)optimize,, *note solveSOS:
        solveSOS,, *note sosdecTernary: sosdecTernary,, *note sosInIdeal:
        sosInIdeal,, or *note lowerBound: lowerBound,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Verbosity: solveSOS_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVerbosity=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value 0, control the level of information printed

Description
===========

This method tests whether various functions work properly using a specified
solver. The most basic invocation uses only the name of the solver. This runs
all tests with that solver and prints a summary. All tests should pass for CSDP
and MOSEK.



See also
========

  * *note Solver: (SemidefiniteProgramming)Solver, -- picking a semidefinite
    programming solver

Ways to use checkSolver:
========================

  * "checkSolver(String)"
  * "checkSolver(String,Function)"
  * "checkSolver(String,String)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note checkSolver: checkSolver, is a *note method function with
options: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

