clean(RR,SOSPoly) -- remove squares with very small coefficients from a sum of squares
**************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note clean: (Macaulay2Doc)clean,
  * Usage: 
        clean (tol, s)
  * Inputs:
      * tol, a *note real number: (Macaulay2Doc)RR,, the tolerance for the
        coefficients.
      * s, an instance of the type *note SOSPoly: SOSPoly,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note SOSPoly: SOSPoly,, a cleaned up *note
        SOSPoly: SOSPoly,

Description
===========

Given a *note sum-of-squares: SOSPoly, polynomial with real coefficients in the
reals, this method removes the squares with coefficients smaller than the given
tolerance. It does nothing on inputs with rational coefficients.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = RR[x,y];                                  |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : s = sosPoly(R, {x^2+.0001*x+1, y}, {2, .0001})|
|                                                   |
|         2              2            2             |
|o2 = 2*(x  + .0001x + 1)  + .0001*(y)              |
|                                                   |
|o2 : SOSPoly                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : clean( .001, s )                              |
|                                                   |
|         2     2                                   |
|o3 = 2*(x  + 1)                                    |
|                                                   |
|o3 : SOSPoly                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------+


See also
========

  * *note SOSPoly: SOSPoly, -- A type to store sums-of-squares polynomials

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note clean(RR,SOSPoly): clean_lpRR_cmSOSPoly_rp, -- remove squares with
    very small coefficients from a sum of squares
