recoverSolution -- factor a rank one positive semidefinite matrix
*****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        sol = recoverSolution(mon,X)
        sol = recoverSolution(sdpsol)
  * Inputs:
      * mon, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, of monomials
      * X, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the moment matrix
      * sdpsol, an instance of the type *note SDPResult: SDPResult,, 
  * Outputs:
      * sol, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the optimal solution

Description
===========

This method attempts to find the optimizing solutions of a sum-of-squares
problem by checking if the moment matrix is rank one.  In this case it
factorizes the matrix and returns the defining vector.

+------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = RR[x,y];                               |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : mon = matrix {{1},{x},{y}};                |
|                                                |
|             3      1                           |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                            |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : X = matrix(RR, {{1,0,1},{0,0,0},{1,0,1}} );|
|                                                |
|                3         3                     |
|o3 : Matrix RR    <-- RR                        |
|              53        53                      |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : sol = recoverSolution(mon,X)               |
|                                                |
|o4 = {x => 0, y => 1}                           |
|                                                |
|o4 : List                                       |
+------------------------------------------------+

See *note lowerBound: lowerBound, for how to use it to find a point realizing a
lower bound.



