solveSOS(...,Solver=>...) -- picking a semidefinite programming solver
**********************************************************************

Description
===========

Macaulay2 has a powerful solver already configured.  If necessary you can use
this variable to change the semidefinite programming solver used in the
background.  See *note Solver: (SemidefiniteProgramming)Solver, for details.

Functions with optional argument named Solver:
==============================================

  * "optimize(...,Solver=>...)" -- see *note Solver:
    (SemidefiniteProgramming)Solver, -- picking a semidefinite programming
    solver
  * "lowerBound(...,Solver=>...)"
  * *note solveSOS(...,Solver=>...):
    solveSOS_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSolver=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, -- picking a semidefinite
    programming solver
  * "sosdecTernary(...,Solver=>...)"
  * "sosInIdeal(...,Solver=>...)"

Further information
===================

  * Default value: null
  * Function: *note solveSOS: solveSOS, -- solve a sum-of-squares problem
  * Option key: *note Solver: (SemidefiniteProgramming)Solver, -- picking a
    semidefinite programming solver
